module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Adequate.AdequateModules.CechExactAffineSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Adequate.AdequateModules.Cohomology
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.BigSites.CoveringSieveMembership

/-!
# The `τ`-sheaf condition of a chosen big site along a covered morphism

A sheaf of modules on a chosen big `τ`-site over `S` carries, with no hypothesis at all, the
sheaf condition for the topology of the site: that is the field
`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.isSheaf`. What the library had no way to do was to *produce* a
covering sieve of that topology from a `τ`-covering family of the site, so the sheaf condition
could not be evaluated anywhere. This module supplies that producer and the two consequences
that the Čech condition of [Stacks, Tag 06VH] needs.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Adequate.BigSite.HasFactoringCovering` — a morphism `g : X ⟶ T` of the site is
  *covered* when some `τ`-covering family of the site factors through it. This is weaker than
  asking `g` itself to be a `τ`-covering morphism, and it is the form in which the morphism
  `Spec(C ⊗_A A') ⟶ Spec C` of the source's proof of [Stacks, Tag 06VI] is covered: there
  `A' = A'₁ × ⋯ × A'ₘ` is the product of a standard affine `τ`-covering of [Stacks, Tag 06VB],
  so `Spec(C ⊗_A A')` is the disjoint union of the `Spec(C ⊗_A A'ⱼ)` and the family of those
  over `Spec C` is a base change of the given `τ`-covering.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Adequate.sieve_generate_mem_topology_of_coveringMorphismProperty` — **the sieve
  generated by a `τ`-covering family of a chosen big site is a covering sieve of the site.**
* `Stacks.Adequate.sieve_generate_singleton_mem_topology_of_hasFactoringCovering` — the sieve
  generated by a covered morphism is a covering sieve of the site.
* `Stacks.Adequate.isSheafFor_singleton_of_hasFactoringCovering` — the singleton sheaf
  condition along a covered morphism, for any sheaf of the site's own topology.
* `Stacks.Adequate.isSheaf_forget_presheaf` — the presheaf of types underlying a sheaf of
  modules on the site is a sheaf for the site's topology. This is the field
  `CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.isSheaf` composed with the forgetful functor, so it is
  unconditional.
* `Stacks.Adequate.cechExactOn_affineSectionFunctor_of_hasFactoringCovering` — **the Čech
  condition of [Stacks, Tag 06VH] for the affine-section functor, from the `τ`-sheaf condition
  alone.**

## Implementation notes

**Why this is not a corollary of the fpqc route.** The library already derives the singleton
sheaf condition from the fpqc sheaf condition of the site, by
`Stacks.Adequate.isAffineSingletonSheaf_of_isSheaf_fpqc` through
`Stacks.Adequate.sieve_generate_singleton_mem_fpqc`. That route asks for descent along an
*arbitrary* flat surjective morphism of affines of the site, which is an fpqc covering but
need not be a `τ`-covering, and the fpqc sheaf condition for a module given only as adequate is
not available — see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Adequate/AdequateModules/BigSiteFpqcSheafCriterion.lean`. The
route here asks only for the `τ`-sheaf condition, which every sheaf of modules on the site has
by definition, at the price of the morphism being covered by a `τ`-covering family rather than
merely faithfully flat. For the morphisms the Čech condition of the source's proof of
[Stacks, Tag 06VI] is applied to, that price is not a price: those morphisms are base changes
of the standard affine `τ`-covering the proof starts from.

**Where the hypothesis is discharged.** `Stacks.Adequate.BigSite.HasFactoringCovering` is a
hypothesis of `Stacks.Adequate.cechExactOn_affineSectionFunctor_of_hasFactoringCovering`, not a
conclusion of this module. It is discharged at `A' = A'₁ × ⋯ × A'ₘ`, the product of a finite
standard affine `τ`-covering of [Stacks, Tag 06VB], by
`Stacks.Adequate.hasFactoringCovering_of_proj` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Adequate/AdequateModules/CechExactStandardCovering.lean`, which
also states the resulting Čech condition there with no hypothesis, as
`Stacks.Adequate.cechExactOn_affineSectionFunctor_pi`. That discharge needs *only* the
projections `A' ⟶ A'ⱼ` of the product, so neither the identification
`C ⊗_A (A'₁ × ⋯ × A'ₘ) ≅ (C ⊗_A A'₁) × ⋯ × (C ⊗_A A'ₘ)` nor `AlgebraicGeometry.specPiIso` is
involved: the factoring morphism out of `Spec(C ⊗_A A'ⱼ)` comes from the universal property of
the pushout `C ⊗_A A'` itself, and the family of its composites with `Spec(C ⊗_A A') ⟶ Spec C`
is the base change of the given covering along `Spec C ⟶ Spec A`.

**Where this sits in `Stacks.Adequate.StandardAffineDescent`.** It supplies the Čech-exactness
hypothesis `hexact`, which is what this module reduces to the `τ`-sheaf condition and which
`Stacks.Adequate.cechExactOn_affineSectionFunctor_pi` then states outright. The rest of that
predicate is the port of [Stacks, Tag 06VB] and [Stacks, Tag 06VH] —
`AdequateFunctor.isAdequate_of_descent` and
`AdequateFunctor.adequateFunctorProductEquivalence` — from all algebras over the base ring to
the algebras of the site, together with the identification of `F_{F, A'}` with the product of
the `F_{F, A'ⱼ}`, and those are supplied in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Adequate/AdequateModules/StandardAffineDescentReduction.lean`
and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Adequate/AdequateModules/StandardAffineProductAdequacy.lean`,
so `StandardAffineDescent` is a theorem; see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Adequate/AdequateModules/AffineLocal.lean`.

The index type of the factoring family is `Type u`, the universe of the schemes, which is where
the index type of a coproduct of schemes of `Scheme.{u}` lives; the covering produced by
`Stacks.Adequate.BigSite.affineCovCofinal` is indexed in `Type 0` and
`Stacks.Adequate.sieve_generate_mem_topology_of_coveringMorphismProperty` is stated at an
arbitrary index universe, so neither is constrained by this choice.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached. The sieve-membership statement is the content of
[Stacks, Tag 03WV] and its four siblings, which are structure fields of the five accepted big
sites, read through `Stacks.Adequate.BigSite.chosen`; the Čech statement is
`Stacks.Adequate.cechExactOn_affineSectionFunctor` with its hypothesis supplied, and that
theorem already carries what Tag 06VH asks of it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 06VH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06VH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06VI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06VI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06VB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06VB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03WV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03WV)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe w v u m

namespace Stacks.Adequate

variable {τ : CoveringTopology} {S : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### Covering sieves from `τ`-covering families -/

/-- **A `τ`-covering family of a chosen big site generates a covering sieve of the site.** If
every member of a family `fᵢ : Xᵢ ⟶ T` of the site is a `τ`-covering morphism of schemes and
the members are jointly surjective, the sieve the family generates belongs to `B.topology`.

This is the eliminator for the field `Stacks.Adequate.BigSite.chosen` — five cases, each
transporting the topology along the equality of the two cutoffs — applied to
`AlgebraicGeometry.sieve₀_mem_overTopology_of_coveringMorphismProperty`, which is the same
statement for a localized big site, uniformly in `τ`. -/
public theorem sieve_generate_mem_topology_of_coveringMorphismProperty (B : BigSite τ S)
    {T : B.category} {I : Type w} (X : I → B.category) (f : ∀ i, X i ⟶ T)
    (hprop : ∀ i, coveringMorphismProperty τ (B.toOver.map (f i)).left)
    (hsurj : ∀ x : T.left.obj, ∃ i, x ∈ Set.range (B.toOver.map (f i)).left) :
    Sieve.generate (Presieve.ofArrows X f) ∈ B.topology T := by
  obtain ⟨cut, base_mem, J, isSheaf, chosen⟩ := B
  rcases chosen with ⟨hτ, C, hC, he, hJ⟩ | ⟨hτ, C, hC, he, hJ⟩ | ⟨hτ, C, hC, he, hJ⟩ |
    ⟨hτ, C, hC, he, hJ⟩ | ⟨hτ, C, hC, he, hJ⟩
  all_goals
    subst hτ; subst he; obtain rfl := eq_of_heq hJ
    first
    | exact sieve₀_mem_overTopology_of_coveringMorphismProperty .zariski C S hC ⟨I, X, f⟩ hprop
        hsurj
    | exact sieve₀_mem_overTopology_of_coveringMorphismProperty .etale C S hC ⟨I, X, f⟩ hprop
        hsurj
    | exact sieve₀_mem_overTopology_of_coveringMorphismProperty .fppf C S hC ⟨I, X, f⟩ hprop
        hsurj
    | exact sieve₀_mem_overTopology_of_coveringMorphismProperty .smooth C S hC ⟨I, X, f⟩ hprop
        hsurj
    | exact sieve₀_mem_overTopology_of_coveringMorphismProperty .syntomic C S hC ⟨I, X, f⟩ hprop
        hsurj

/-- **The standard affine `τ`-coverings of a chosen big site are cofinal**, and the topology
membership that `Stacks.Adequate.BigSite.standardAffineCov` carries as subtype data is
*derived*: every covering sieve of an affine object of the site is refined by a standard affine
`τ`-covering of that object, which generates a covering sieve of the site.

This is `Stacks.Adequate.BigSite.StandardCovCofinal`, the hypothesis `hCovCofinal` of
[Stacks, Tag 03F9] at the standard affine coverings, discharged. It is [Stacks, Tag 03XA] read
through the five-way eliminator for the field `Stacks.Adequate.BigSite.chosen`: cofinality on a
localized big site is `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isOverStandardCovering_sieve₀_le` and the sieve
membership of the refinement is `AlgebraicGeometry.IsOverStandardCovering.sieve₀_mem_overTopology`.

The sibling `Stacks.Adequate.BigSite.affineCovCofinal` is the same statement for the weaker
collection `Stacks.Adequate.BigSite.affineCov`, whose members are only required to be jointly
surjective families of `τ`-covering morphisms between affines; this one retains the standard
affine shape of [Stacks, Tag 03X9], which is what the Čech comparison of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Adequate/AdequateModules/Cohomology.lean` is stated at. -/
public theorem BigSite.standardAffineCovCofinal (B : BigSite τ S) : B.StandardCovCofinal := by
  obtain ⟨cut, base_mem, J, isSheaf, chosen⟩ := B
  rcases chosen with ⟨hτ, C, hC, he, hJ⟩ | ⟨hτ, C, hC, he, hJ⟩ | ⟨hτ, C, hC, he, hJ⟩ |
    ⟨hτ, C, hC, he, hJ⟩ | ⟨hτ, C, hC, he, hJ⟩
  all_goals
    subst hτ; subst he; obtain rfl := eq_of_heq hJ
    intro U hU R hR
    first
    | (obtain ⟨E, hEstd, hER⟩ := exists_isOverStandardCovering_sieve₀_le .zariski C S hC hU hR
       exact ⟨⟨E, IsOverStandardCovering.sieve₀_mem_overTopology .zariski C S hC E hEstd⟩,
         hEstd, hER⟩)
    | (obtain ⟨E, hEstd, hER⟩ := exists_isOverStandardCovering_sieve₀_le .etale C S hC hU hR
       exact ⟨⟨E, IsOverStandardCovering.sieve₀_mem_overTopology .etale C S hC E hEstd⟩,
         hEstd, hER⟩)
    | (obtain ⟨E, hEstd, hER⟩ := exists_isOverStandardCovering_sieve₀_le .fppf C S hC hU hR
       exact ⟨⟨E, IsOverStandardCovering.sieve₀_mem_overTopology .fppf C S hC E hEstd⟩,
         hEstd, hER⟩)
    | (obtain ⟨E, hEstd, hER⟩ := exists_isOverStandardCovering_sieve₀_le .smooth C S hC hU hR
       exact ⟨⟨E, IsOverStandardCovering.sieve₀_mem_overTopology .smooth C S hC E hEstd⟩,
         hEstd, hER⟩)
    | (obtain ⟨E, hEstd, hER⟩ := exists_isOverStandardCovering_sieve₀_le .syntomic C S hC hU hR
       exact ⟨⟨E, IsOverStandardCovering.sieve₀_mem_overTopology .syntomic C S hC E hEstd⟩,
         hEstd, hER⟩)

/-! ### Covered morphisms -/

/-- A morphism `g : X ⟶ T` of a chosen big site is *covered* when some `τ`-covering family of
the site factors through it: a family `kᵢ : Yᵢ ⟶ X` such that the composites `kᵢ ≫ g` are
`τ`-covering morphisms of schemes and are jointly surjective.

A `τ`-covering morphism is covered, by the one-member family of its identity. The morphism
`Spec(C ⊗_A A') ⟶ Spec C` of the source's proof of [Stacks, Tag 06VI] is covered without being
a `τ`-covering morphism, `Spec(C ⊗_A A')` being a disjoint union of the members of one. -/
public def BigSite.HasFactoringCovering (B : BigSite τ S) {X T : B.category} (g : X ⟶ T) :
    Prop :=
  ∃ (I : Type u) (Y : I → B.category) (k : ∀ i, Y i ⟶ X),
    (∀ i, coveringMorphismProperty τ (B.toOver.map (k i ≫ g)).left) ∧
      ∀ x : T.left.obj, ∃ i, x ∈ Set.range (B.toOver.map (k i ≫ g)).left

/-- A `τ`-covering morphism of a chosen big site is covered: the one-member family of its
identity factors through it. -/
public theorem BigSite.hasFactoringCovering_of_coveringMorphismProperty (B : BigSite τ S)
    {X T : B.category} (g : X ⟶ T)
    (hprop : coveringMorphismProperty τ (B.toOver.map g).left)
    (hsurj : ∀ x : T.left.obj, ∃ _ : PUnit.{u + 1}, x ∈ Set.range (B.toOver.map g).left) :
    B.HasFactoringCovering g :=
  ⟨PUnit.{u + 1}, fun _ => X, fun _ => 𝟙 X,
    fun _ => by rwa [Category.id_comp], fun x => by simpa using hsurj x⟩

/-- **The sieve generated by a covered morphism is a covering sieve of the site.** The sieve
generated by a factoring `τ`-covering family is a covering sieve by
`Stacks.Adequate.sieve_generate_mem_topology_of_coveringMorphismProperty`, and it is contained
in the sieve generated by the morphism, every member of the family factoring through it. -/
public theorem sieve_generate_singleton_mem_topology_of_hasFactoringCovering (B : BigSite τ S)
    {X T : B.category} {g : X ⟶ T} (hg : B.HasFactoringCovering g) :
    Sieve.generate (Presieve.singleton g) ∈ B.topology T := by
  obtain ⟨I, Y, k, hprop, hsurj⟩ := hg
  refine B.topology.superset_covering ?_
    (sieve_generate_mem_topology_of_coveringMorphismProperty B Y (fun i => k i ≫ g) hprop hsurj)
  rw [Sieve.generate_le_iff, Presieve.ofArrows_le_iff]
  intro i
  exact (Sieve.generate (Presieve.singleton g)).downward_closed
    (Sieve.le_generate _ _ _ (Presieve.singleton_self g)) (k i)

/-- **The singleton sheaf condition along a covered morphism.** A presheaf of types satisfying
the sheaf condition for the topology of the site satisfies it for the one-member presieve of a
covered morphism, that presieve generating a covering sieve. -/
public theorem isSheafFor_singleton_of_hasFactoringCovering (B : BigSite τ S)
    {P : B.categoryᵒᵖ ⥤ Type v} (hP : Presieve.IsSheaf B.topology P)
    {X T : B.category} {g : X ⟶ T} (hg : B.HasFactoringCovering g) :
    Presieve.IsSheafFor P (Presieve.singleton g) :=
  (Presieve.isSheafFor_iff_generate _).2
    (hP _ (sieve_generate_singleton_mem_topology_of_hasFactoringCovering B hg))

/-! ### The Čech condition from the `τ`-sheaf condition -/

/-- The presheaf of types underlying a sheaf of modules on a chosen big site satisfies the sheaf
condition for the topology of the site. This is the field
`CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.isSheaf` of the sheaf of modules, composed with the forgetful
functor to types, and so holds with no hypothesis. -/
public theorem isSheaf_forget_presheaf (B : BigSite τ S)
    (F : SheafOfModules.{max u m} B.structureSheaf) :
    Presieve.IsSheaf B.topology
      (F.val.presheaf ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget AddCommGrpCat.{max u m}) := by
  rw [← isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type]
  exact GrothendieckTopology.HasSheafCompose.isSheaf _ F.isSheaf

/-- **The Čech condition of [Stacks, Tag 06VH] for the affine-section functor, from the
`τ`-sheaf condition of the site alone.**

`Stacks.Adequate.cechExactOn_affineSectionFunctor` reduces the Čech condition to the one-member
sheaf condition for the base changes `Spec(C₁) ⟶ Spec(C₀)` of `Spec A' ⟶ Spec A`, and
`Stacks.Adequate.isSheafFor_singleton_of_hasFactoringCovering` supplies that from the sheaf
condition `F` carries by definition, as soon as each of those morphisms is covered by a
`τ`-covering family of the site.

This replaces the hypotheses of
`Stacks.Adequate.cechExactOn_affineSectionFunctor_of_isAffineSingletonSheaf` — the fpqc sheaf
condition in the shape `Stacks.Adequate.IsAffineSingletonSheaf`, together with flatness and
surjectivity of the base-changed morphisms — by a condition on the covering alone. Nothing
about `F` beyond `CategoryTheory.SheafOfModules.isSheaf` is used, so no sheaf condition for `F`
is assumed and in particular [Stacks, Tag 03O1] is not invoked. -/
public theorem cechExactOn_affineSectionFunctor_of_hasFactoringCovering (B : BigSite τ S)
    (F : SheafOfModules.{max u m} B.structureSheaf)
    (A : CommRingCat.{u}) (f : Spec A ⟶ S)
    (A' : AdequateFunctor.AlgebrasInSite A (schemeSizeBelow B.cutoff))
    (hcov : ∀ {C₀ C₁ : AdequateFunctor.AlgebrasInSite A (schemeSizeBelow B.cutoff)}
      (iB : C₀ ⟶ C₁) (iA : A' ⟶ C₁),
      IsColimit (BinaryCofan.mk
        ((AdequateFunctor.siteAlgebraInclusion A (schemeSizeBelow B.cutoff)).map iB)
        ((AdequateFunctor.siteAlgebraInclusion A (schemeSizeBelow B.cutoff)).map iA)) →
      B.HasFactoringCovering ((affineSpecOver B A f).map iB.op)) :
    AdequateFunctor.CechExactOn
      (AdequateFunctor.siteAlgebraInclusion A (schemeSizeBelow B.cutoff))
      (affineSectionFunctor B F A f) A' :=
  cechExactOn_affineSectionFunctor B F A f A' fun iB iA hc =>
    isSheafFor_singleton_of_hasFactoringCovering B (isSheaf_forget_presheaf B F) (hcov iB iA hc)

end Stacks.Adequate

end
